(a) the current operational status of NavIC constellation, including the number of satellites presently providing Position, Navigation and Timing (PNT) services;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of failures of imported atomic clocks on the operational capability of NavIC constellation and if so, the outcomes thereof;
(c) the present status of deployment of indigenous space-grade rubidium atomic clocks in NavIC constellation; and
(d) the updated timeline for the launch of remaining second-generation NavIC satellites and for restoring the constellation to its full operational capability?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of AI, automation and other emerging technologies on occupations covered under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY), ITIs and other Skill India schemes;
(b) the trades or job roles identified as being at risk of significant transformation or displacement and the details thereof; and
(c) whether such assessment has been used to revise qualification packs, training curricula, reskilling programmes and future skill demand projections under Skill India and the details thereof?

(a) the number of accident black spots identified on National Highways in Tamil Nadu, along with the number permanently rectified, temporarily rectified and pending rectification, as of the latest available date;
(b) the details of road safety audits, engineering improvements and pedestrian safety measures undertaken or sanctioned on National Highways in Tamil Nadu during the last three years; and
(c) the timeline for completing the rectification of the remaining identified black spots and implementing the pending road safety improvement works in Tamil Nadu?

(a) the major infrastructure projects identified for the Chennai–Kamarajar–Cuddalore Port Cluster under the Maritime Amrit Kaal Vision, 2047;
(b) the project-wise investment, year-wise implementation timeline, capacity addition envisaged and performance benchmarks, including cargo throughput, turnaround time, logistics cost reduction, private investment mobilisation and export competitiveness; and
(c) the measures taken to integrate the cluster with industrial corridors, multimodal logistics infrastructure and export-oriented manufacturing, along with the expected increase in cargo handling capacity and employment generation?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comparative assessment of health warning and labelling requirements for food products manufactured and sold in the country and abroad, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the health warnings or mandatory disclosures required under the regulations of the United States and the European Union, but not under FSSAI regulations;
(c) whether Government has examined aligning FSSAI health warning and labelling requirements with global standards, including those of the United States and the European Union, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of Atal Tinkering Labs operational in the State of Tamil Nadu and the funds disbursed to the State under the Atal Innovation Mission to date;
(b) whether Government has developed a framework to assess the outcomes of Atal Tinkering Labs, including student innovation projects, patents, prototypes, start-ups and other measurable indicators; and
(c) whether such outcome data is maintained State-wise, including for Tamil Nadu, and if so, the details thereof, and if not, whether Government proposes to institute such tracking?

(a) the present status of the liquidation and disposal proceedings of Hindustan Photo Films Manufacturing Company Limited (HPF), Ooty;
(b) whether Government has formulated any plan for the utilisation or redevelopment of the Company's land, buildings and other infrastructure following the completion of the liquidation process, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has examined the feasibility of repurposing the HPF campus to support India's creative economy, including film preservation and restoration, media technology, animation, skill development or other allied activities, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of candidates who received offers, joined and completed internships under the PM Internship Scheme since its inception, district-wise in Tamil Nadu;
(b) the number of internship opportunities offered under the Scheme in Tamil Nadu, company-wise;
(c) the details of companies participating in the Scheme in Tamil Nadu, including the districts where internships are offered;
(d) the expenditure incurred on publicity and advertisement of the Scheme, year-wise; and
(e) the steps being taken to improve implementation of the Scheme and expand internship opportunities in Tamil Nadu?

